-- The invitation's single-use token, stored as its SHA-256 (ADR-0067 §2,
-- amended 2026-09-04 — the operator's answer to the finding `D15.1`
-- escalated, taken while the D15 window is open). Generated by drizzle-kit as
-- a bare `ADD COLUMN … NOT NULL` and widened here, before it was ever
-- committed, into the four statements a table that may already hold rows
-- needs: an `ADD COLUMN … NOT NULL` with no default fails outright against one.
--
-- Nothing writes `organization_invitations` in this repository yet — the
-- create path is `D15.3`'s — so on a clean tree statement 2 touches nothing.
-- It exists for the fork or the hand-loaded database that does hold rows, and
-- for that case the value matters: see its own comment.
--
-- Neither the column nor the unique index is expected to block (the
-- `db-schema-change` rule for a migrator that runs everything in one
-- transaction, ADR-0060 §5): the table is new as of `0011` and empty.
ALTER TABLE "organization_invitations" ADD COLUMN "token_hash" text;--> statement-breakpoint
-- A sentinel, unpresentable by construction, for a row that predates the
-- column. Deliberately **not** a hash: `token_hash` holds
-- `sha256Base64url(token)`, which is always 43 characters of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`,
-- and `unminted:<uuid>` is longer and contains a `:` — so it cannot be the
-- digest of anything a caller can present, and such a row is
-- unacceptable-by-token while staying acceptable-by-address exactly as it was.
--
-- A fresh uuid rather than this row's own id, although the id would be
-- deterministic: the idempotency here comes from `WHERE token_hash IS NULL`
-- and not from the value (unlike `0012`, where the derived slug must *match*
-- on replay), and a value derived from the id would be reconstructible by
-- anyone holding it — the id is a URL segment on
-- `POST /user/invitations/:id/accept`. That only bites under a bug that
-- compared a client's value against this column without hashing it, and
-- costing nothing to remove is reason enough to remove it.
UPDATE "organization_invitations" SET "token_hash" = 'unminted:' || gen_random_uuid()::text WHERE "token_hash" IS NULL;--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "organization_invitations" ALTER COLUMN "token_hash" SET NOT NULL;--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "organization_invitations" ADD CONSTRAINT "organization_invitations_token_hash_unique" UNIQUE("token_hash");
